+# Custom Match rooms (カスタムマッチ) — exvs2-lobbies, 2026-11-17
+
+Status: **card-server handlers built and tested locally (fake cards). Not deployed. Not tried on a real LM yet.**
+
+## What the game sends
+
+| Request | Fields (exe descriptor, `analysis/proto/from_exe/game_server_nue.proto`) | Reply |
+|---|---|---|
+| `LoadRoom` (418), LM "カスタムマッチのルーム検索" after a card touch | `is_card`, `access_code`, `chip_id`, `mucha_country_code` | `load_room {pilot_id, is_new_card, rooms[RoomGroup], status, acid_error}` |
+| `RegisterRoom` (419), LM, a room picked from that list | `pilot_id`, `room_id` (= RoomGroup.tag_id), `tag_type` | `register_room {status}` (required) |
+| `PreLoadCard` (cabinet, every credit) | — | optional `matching_tag {id, tag_name, tag_type, matching_type, end_date, matching_attribute, world_id, rule_type, …}` |
+
+`RoomGroup` required fields: `tag_id`, `registration_code`, `tag_type`, `matching_type`, `start_date`, `end_date`,
+`class_id_min`, `class_id_max`; optional `current_num`, `member_limit`, win-rate / grade bounds, `rule_type`,
+`fes_rule_type`, `policy`.
+
+Before this branch the server answered both with `ErrServer "Unhandled case"`, and the LM showed
+"このカードは使用できません" (this card cannot be used).
+
+## Flow (vsmobile replaced by the launcher)
+
+1. **Make a room** (launcher → its card server → matchmaker `POST /tag/rooms`): owner pilot id, solo/team
+   (`matchingType` 1/2), MS restriction (`tagType` 1/2), rule, member limit. Reply has the 6-character room code.
+2. **Join** (`POST /tag/rooms/join {code, pilotId}`): friends type the code in their launcher.
+3. **LM room search** (LoadRoom): the card is looked up like LoadMeetingCard (access code + chip id; unknown card →
+   ErrServer as before). The reply lists the rooms the card joined today. No rooms → a valid empty list.
+4. **LM pick** (RegisterRoom): the registry records "pilot X plays room Y today" if X is a member (status 0), else status 1.
+5. **Next credit** (PreLoadCard, only with `CustomRooms.SendMatchingTag=true`): `matching_tag` carries the room id and
+   `world_id` (6 solo / 7 team by default, or the room's own world). The cabinet's world override is static analysis
+   only (`casual-shuffle-matching.md` §2: mode codes 3–6 take the server world at +0x71c when +0x718 == 3).
+6. Rooms close at the day reset (`DayResetHour`, `TimeZone`; default local midnight). Picks go with them.
+
+No public-queue fallback and no CPU fill: a room world is a hard bucket in the matchmaker (6, 7, 24, 26, 27, 32, 33).
+
+## Where the registry lives
+
+* `Matchmaking/CustomRoomStore.cs`: in-memory + `custom_rooms.json`, wire pilot ids only (no card secrets), codes
+  logged masked (`AB****`).
+* Served by `Controllers/CustomRoomController.cs` under `/tag/rooms` on the matchmaker process, so the existing
+  `SecurityGuardMiddleware` rules apply (X-Tag-Secret, LAN-only without a secret, per-IP rate limit).
+* Card servers reach it through `ICustomRoomClient`: `HttpCustomRoomClient` when `OnlineTag.InviteUrl` /
+  `OnlineMatching.MatchUrl` is set, else in-process. `CustomRooms.LocalStore=true` forces in-process (single-PC test
+  where only the card server exe is swapped). Registry down → LoadRoom answers an empty list, RegisterRoom status 1.
+
+API (all JSON, camelCase; logical outcomes are 200 `{status, room}`):
+
+| Method | Path | Body / reply |
+|---|---|---|
+| POST | `/tag/rooms` | `{ownerPilotId, ownerName, name, matchingType, tagType, ruleType, worldId, memberLimit}` |
+| POST | `/tag/rooms/join` | `{code, pilotId}` |
+| POST | `/tag/rooms/leave` | `{code, pilotId}` (owner leaving closes the room) |
+| POST | `/tag/rooms/register` | `{pilotId, roomId}` |
+| GET | `/tag/rooms/pilot/{pilotId}` | rooms the pilot can enter today |
+| GET | `/tag/rooms/pilot/{pilotId}/selected` | today's pick or 204 |
+| GET | `/tag/rooms/{code}` | room summary without member ids |
+
+## Config (`CardServerConfig.CustomRooms`)
+
+| Key | Default | Meaning |
+|---|---|---|
+| `Enabled` | true | answer 418/419 (false = old Unhandled reply) |
+| `LocalStore` | false | keep the registry in this process |
+| `StateFile` | `custom_rooms.json` | registry state |
+| `SendMatchingTag` | **false** | EXPERIMENTAL PreLoadCard.matching_tag for today's pick |
+| `SoloWorldId` / `TeamWorldId` | 6 / 7 | default world_id |
+| `DayResetHour` / `TimeZone` | 0 / local | room expiry |
+| `MaxMembers`, `MaxRoomsPerOwner`, `MaxRoomsPerPilot` | 32, 3, 10 | limits |
+| `ClassIdMin` / `ClassIdMax` | 1 / 4 | RoomGroup class bounds (Pilot … Over) |
+
+## Open questions (need the real LM / cabinet)
+
+1. Does the LM accept `status = 0` / `acid_error = ACID_SUCCESS` as OK for LoadRoom, and `status = 0` for RegisterRoom?
+   (Assumed; no LM-side code was read. The LM binary is not on the box.)
+2. What does the LM show for an empty list (a "no rooms" message is expected) and for a new (unregistered) card
+   (`is_new_card = true`, no rooms)?
+3. Units of `start_date` / `end_date` (sent as Unix seconds like other `end_date` fields) and whether the LM hides a
+   room whose window does not include "now".
+4. `win_rate_*`, `grade_*`, `policy` are not sent; if the LM requires them for display, add them.
+5. Which world and attr2 the cabinet really uses after a `matching_tag` (watch MMS `EntryMatching` world/attr2 in the
+   log with `SendMatchingTag=true`). If attr2 is not the room id, two rooms of the same type would share a bucket and
+   the matchmaker needs a room key (next step below).
+
+## Next steps (not built)
+
+* **Matchmaker room key**: when a cabinet enters a tag world, look up its am_id's pick in `CustomRoomStore` and add
+  the room id to the hard bucket key, so two rooms never mix even if attr2 is the same.
+* **Launcher room UI** (Windows WPF + Linux): a "Custom room" panel with *Create* (solo/team, MS restriction, limit) →
+  shows the code with a copy button; *Join* (code box); *My rooms today* (list, leave/close). The launcher talks to its
+  local card server, which adds the card's wire pilot id and forwards to `/tag/rooms` with the shared secret (the
+  launcher never holds the secret). Card-server side endpoint for that: `/ui/rooms/*` scoped to the signed-in card.
+* Vsmobile-style public/event rooms (daily schedule) would be server-made rooms with every pilot treated as a member.
+
+## Tests
+
+* `Tests/Matchmaking.Tests/CustomRoomTests.cs` (20): store, expiry/zone, persistence, LM reply wire layout
+  (field 1418 bytes), strict round trips, matching_tag, in-process client.
+* `server-sketch/loadtest/custom_room_e2e.py` (exvs2-lobbies repo): real server, fake cards, strict proto2 parse with
+  the exe schema; 15/15 in-process, 15/15 with the registry on a separate matchmaker, plus registry-down fallback.
