+Two places carry room settings:
+
+* **LM** — `LoadRoom` reply, one `RoomGroup` per room (callback `0x1408e7970`, filter/copy `0x1408bd1cc`, private
+  panel `0x140a29c20`). Display + list filter only.
+* **Cab** — `PreLoadCard.matching_tag` for the room the card picked on the LM (copied by `0x1406cd510` from
+  PreLoadCard+0x50 into card+0xb70, "T" below). This is what changes matching / battle.
+
+## LM: LoadRoom.RoomGroup
+
+| Field (#) | Values | LM shows | Enforced? | Server | Conf. |
+|---|---|---|---|---|---|
+| tag_id (1) | room id | — (sent back in RegisterRoom) | — | room id | H |
+| registration_code | 6 chars | not shown on the LM | — | code | H |
+| tag_type | 2 private (list, ≤ 7), 4 public (single slot: time, mode, class only); 1/3 skipped | which list | yes (filter) | kind (2/4; stored 1 → 2) | H |
+| matching_type | 1 SOLO (shuffle), 2 TEAM, 3 MIX | mode text | display | mode | H |
+| start_date / end_date | Unix s | `HH:MM~HH:MM` (LM local time) | yes: room hidden outside the window | opens / closes | H |
+| current_num / member_limit | | `n/limit` | display | members / max players | H |
+| class_id_min/max | 1 Pilot, 2 Valiant, 3 Ace, 4 Over (default 1/4) | class icons | display only | class from / to | H (ids M) |
+| grade_id_min/max | 1..11 (default 1/11) | grade in the class icon ("Pilot 10 ~ Extreme 00" for defaults) | display only | grade (API; UI uses defaults) | M |
+| win_rate_min (9) / win_rate_max (10) | default 100 / 0; LM prints `#9%~#10%` | win rate | display only | **#9 = upper, #10 = lower** (sent only if not 100/0) | H |
+| rule_type | 0..3 kept, else 0 | Rule_Limited "unit setting rule": ≠0 = あり (on), 0 = なし | display | unit rule switch (UI default **off**) | H |
+| fes_rule_type | 1–7 DUAL, SCORE, BURST, ASCORE, ABOOST, UNLIMIT, MUGEN; 10–14 ONE_0–4; 20–24 ONEXU_0–4; else none | Rule_Fes `RENT_RULE_*` | display (cab uses the matching_tag copy) | fes rule | H (meaning of each rule M) |
+| policy | 1–11 → `CUSTOM_MTCH_MSG_%u` | Rule_Comment preset text (no free text) | display | comment preset | H |
+| is_new_card / status | status must be 1; new card → NOTUSE | | yes | | H |
+
+## Cab: PreLoadCard.matching_tag (T = card+0xb70)
+
+| Field (T+off) | Values | Cab effect | Server | Conf. |
+|---|---|---|---|---|
+| id (+4) | room id | **MMS attr2** for worlds 6–9, 24, 26–33 (table `0x140753ab4`) → one matchmaker bucket per room | room id | H |
+| tag_name (+8, 0x24 bytes) | UTF-8 | card-touch HUD line 2 (`CRD_TCH_CSTM_SET`) | name or code | H |
+| tag_type (+0x28) | 1 EV / 2 PV / 4 PB | HUD line 1 prefix; **world choice** (`0x140822e20`): 1 → world_id from the tag, 2 → fixed 6 solo / 7 team, other → default 26/27 | kind | H |
+| matching_type (+0x2c) | 1/2/3 | HUD SHUFFLE/TEAM/MIX; checked against the sortie (solo vs team) at `0x14074e3fa` | mode | H |
+| matching_attribute (+0x30) | | MMS attr3 (unless oncompe) — not part of the bucket key | 1 | H |
+| world_id (+0x34) | | only honoured for tag_type 1 (event) | 6/7 or config | H |
+| end_date (+0x38) | Unix s | checked at `0x14087749f` (room over → no entry) | closes | H |
+| fes_rule_type (+0x40) | as above | sets fes rule + play sub-mode 3 (`0x140875780`, `0x140875c60`); MS limits with it (`0x140879ed0`) | fes rule (only if set) | H (gameplay L) |
+| timer (+0x44) | seconds, 999 special | overrides the battle timer (`0x14085c71d`) | experimental, only if set | M |
+| revenge_flag (+0x48) | bool | rematch flag for mode codes 3–6 (`0x1407a93ef`) | experimental | M |
+| randomstage_only_flag (+0x49) | bool | random-stage-only flag (`0x1407b613f`) | experimental | M |
+| oncompe_matching_flag (+0x4a) | bool | HUD ROOM_VS, different create seq, no attr3 | always false | M |
+| selectable_ms_id (+0x50) / blocklist (+0x68) | MS ids | usable MS list (`0x1406cebe0` adds selectable when rule_type ≠ 0; `0x140879ed0`) | not sent (all MS usable) | M |
+| rule_type (+0x80) | 0..3 | enables the selectable list above | unit rule switch | M |
+
+## What the server validates (`CustomRoomStore.Validate`)
+
+kind ∈ {1, 2, 4} (web UI: 2/4), mode ∈ {1, 2, 3}, members 2–64 (0 = default), rule 0–3, fes ∈ {0, 1–7, 10–14, 20–24},
+comment 0–11, timer 0–999, class 1–4 with min ≤ max, grade 1–11, win rate 0–100 with lower ≤ upper, name ≤ 36 UTF-8
+bytes, opens < daily reset, closes after opens / now and not after the reset.
+
+## Not possible / not done
+
+* Free-text comments (LM only has 11 presets). Exact preset texts live in the LM string table (`CUSTOM_MTCH_MSG_1..11`);
+  the web UI shows "Preset message n".
+* MS restriction lists (selectable / blocklist) — the layout is known, but the UI does not offer them yet.
+* The game never enforces class / grade / win-rate ranges; the web UI enforces class on join (`EnforceClassRange`).
