+
+---
+
+## 6. Suggested web UI changes
+
+Concrete, in priority order. These are suggestions only (this task does not change the UI).
+
+1. **Comment labels.** Replace “Preset message {n}” / “定型メッセージ {n}” with the official Japanese strings once `CUSTOM_MTCH_MSG_1..11` are dumped from the LM string table. Until then, do not guess IDs. The five known texts to expect in that table are 気楽に対戦, 初心者限定, 誰でも歓迎, 初心者同士楽しもう, 機体練習.
+2. **Class 4 label.** Change Over / オーバー to **Extreme / エクストリーム** (official IB class name). Keep Pilot / Valiant / Ace.
+3. **Mode labels.** JA: ソロ出撃 / チーム出撃 / ミックス出撃 (drop “シャッフル” as the primary solo label, or keep it only as a hint). EN: Solo / Team / Mix.
+4. **Rematch.** Promote リターンマッチ out of the experimental panel, labels **許可 / 禁止** (default 許可, unless we have a reason to default off). Disable the control when a fes rule other than なし is selected.
+5. **Fes rule dropdown.** Default / simple mode: only なし, デュアルセレクト (1), アタックブースト (5), and EXオーバーリミットバトル **once its id is confirmed**. Keep the other protocol values in an advanced list so we do not throw away cab-supported rules, but do not present them as official site options. Rename デュアル → デュアルセレクト, Aブースト / A-Boost → アタックブースト, and the confirmed over-limit id to EXオーバーリミットバトル.
+6. **Max players.** Dropdown **4 / 8 / 16 / 32 / 64**, default 8 or 32 (official default was not on the cropped screenshot). Stop offering 2–3; official custom matching will not start below 4 anyway.
+7. **Schedule.** Add 開催日 (today..+14), 開始時刻 snapped to 10 minutes, optional clamp 07:00–22:50 (or 22:00 — last minute uncertain), and 開催時間 **1 / 3 / 5 hours** that computes `end_date` from `start_date`. Keep “until daily reset” only as an explicit extra, not the default empty end.
+8. **Win rate.** Step of **5**, labels 以上 / 以下 (or “Win rate from / to” with a 5% step). Optionally enforce on join the way official VS.Mobile does (the cab will not).
+9. **Grade range.** Expose `GradeIdMin` / `GradeIdMax` on the form once the 1–11 ↔ 10..1 / ∞ mapping is confirmed from the LM. Do not invent labels before that.
+10. **Visibility vs “Public”.** Do not call player-created `tag_type` 4 “パブリック” as if it were official public rooms. Label it as the **LM public slot** (or drop player-created public rooms). Add a separate “List in room search / ルーム検索に公開する” flag if/when a search page exists.
+11. **Unit restrictions.** If we want official behaviour, add cost (max 2 of 1500/2000/2500/3000), series (max 5), and unit (max 50) pickers that actually fill `selectable_ms_id`, and turn `rule_type` on only when a list is set. The current ON switch with no list is misleading. Preset codes can wait.
+12. **Approval, board, 15/month, paid-only create.** Optional for a private server. If we add approval, it should gate `join` until the owner accepts. A 15/month cap is official flavour, not required.
+13. **Timer / random stage.** Leave in Advanced, keep the “not an official VS.Mobile option / untested” hint. Do not advertise them as custom-room settings from the site.
+14. **Optional name.** Keep it, but hint “cab card-touch label (official VS.Mobile has no room name)”.
+15. **Join copy.** Official term is ルーム招待コード as well as ルームコード. Either is fine; “招待コード” matches the site.
+
+---
+
+## 7. Not found / still uncertain
+
+* Full 11 comment strings and their `CUSTOM_MTCH_MSG` IDs.
+* Official invite-code length and alphabet (no official example published in the pages above).
+* Exact last start time in the 22:00 hour (22:00 only vs 22:50).
+* Which `fes_rule_type` is EXオーバーリミットバトル.
+* `grade_id` mapping onto official grades 10–1 and Extreme ∞ / LM “Extreme 00”.
+* Whether IB still forbids being in more than one room (documented for XB).
+* Whether official public rooms are actually split by class band (wiki only, hedged).
+* Official 機体プリセット設定 and ルーム解散 help bodies (URLs not confirmed; blog used as M).
+* Wayback captures of older `vsmobile.bandainamco-am.co.jp` pages (CDX failed this turn).
+* Timer, random-stage, and stage options as official custom-room settings — no evidence they exist there.
+
+---
+
+## 8. Bottom line
+
+Official IB Custom Match is a **VS.Mobile (and live-monitor) room registry**: paid members schedule a 1/3/5-hour private room up to 14 days ahead, share an invite code or publish to search, optionally require approval, and can restrict who joins and which units may be used. The cab then matches only those members during the window.
+
+Our implementation already has the important protocol fields the LM and cab understand (code, solo/team/mix, time window, class, win rate, fes, 11 comment IDs, rematch flag, unit-rule switch). The web UI does not yet follow the official form on **duration, player-count steps, comment text, Extreme vs Over, rematch placement, fes-rule subset, unit lists, search visibility, approval, or grade**. Those are the mismatches worth fixing if the Rooms page is meant to stand in for VS.Mobile.
