@@ -132,3 +132,15 @@ as picked only once it opens.
 
 This uses the registry's existing `POST /tag/rooms/register` call, so a shared registry (LA) running 00b2619 or
 later needs no update.
+
+## 1on1 fes rooms (matchmaker)
+
+A Custom Match entry carries only the room id (MMS attr2), not the fes rule, so the matchmaker looks the rule up in
+its own room registry (`/tag/rooms` store on the shared matchmaker). A solo entry whose room has a **1on1 fes rule**
+(10–14 "One (0–4)" = 1on1 all cost / 3000 / 2500 / 2000 / 1500, 20–24 "One XU (0–4)" = the same with unlimited EX
+burst) is matched like the Fes 1on1 world: two humans, one per side, no CPU seats, no NOCPU hold. Team entries into
+such a room are refused.
+
+**Dual Select (1) is not 1v1.** Each player picks two MS and chooses one just before the VS screen; it is still a 2v2
+battle, so a solo still needs a partner and `NoCpuPartner` still waits for 4 humans. The same holds for the other
+1–7 rules. Card servers using a remote registry need no change; only the matchmaker hosting the registry does.
